     1,
     "Dear Bloggers,\r<br>\r<br>I am trying to modify some features of my plot (facet wrap with each plot containing two black lines):\r<br>1. have the two lines both black, one of which dashed;\r<br>2. have the plot titles bigger with a white background;\r<br>3. have a legend with title “Forecast Type” and elements “e” and “Box-Cox”;\r<br>\r<br>All the options that I have tried so far either don’t work at all or don’t work together, any suggestion will be welcomed!\r<br>\r<br>Ale\r<br>\r<br>ggplot(new.data,aes(years,value,group=type))+\r<br>  geom_line()+\r<br>  scale_color_manual(name=&quot;Forecast Type&quot;,values=c(&quot;e”=&quot;black&quot;,&quot;Box-Cox”=&quot;black&quot;))+\r<br>  facet_wrap(~area)\r<br>\r<br>structure(list(area = structure(c(12L, 3L, 7L, 5L, 16L, 13L, \r<br>2L, 10L, 17L, 4L, 14L, 8L, 9L, 11L, 1L, 15L, 6L, 12L, 3L, 7L, \r<br>5L, 16L, 13L, 2L, 10L, 17L, 4L, 14L, 8L, 9L, 11L, 1L, 15L, 6L, \r<br>12L, 3L, 7L, 5L, 16L, 13L, 2L, 10L, 17L, 4L, 14L, 8L, 9L, 11L, \r<br>1L, 15L, 6L, 12L, 3L, 7L, 5L, 16L, 13L, 2L, 10L, 17L, 4L, 14L, \r<br>8L, 9L, 11L, 1L, 15L, 6L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 3L, \r<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 5L, 5L, 5L, 5L, 6L, 6L, 6L, 6L, 7L, \r<br>7L, 7L, 7L, 8L, 8L, 8L, 8L, 9L, 9L, 9L, 9L, 10L, 10L, 10L, 10L, \r<br>11L, 11L, 11L, 11L, 12L, 12L, 12L, 12L, 13L, 13L, 13L, 13L, 14L, \r<br>14L, 14L, 14L, 15L, 15L, 15L, 15L, 16L, 16L, 16L, 16L, 17L, 17L, \r<br>17L, 17L), .Label = c(&quot;Andalusia&quot;, &quot;Aragon&quot;, &quot;Asturias&quot;, &quot;Balearic Islands&quot;, \r<br>&quot;Basque Countries&quot;, &quot;Canary Islands&quot;, &quot;Cantabria&quot;, &quot;Castile and Leon&quot;, \r<br>&quot;Castile La Mancha&quot;, &quot;Catalonia&quot;, &quot;Extremadura&quot;, &quot;Galicia&quot;, &quot;La Rioja&quot;, \r<br>&quot;Madrid&quot;, &quot;Murcia&quot;, &quot;Navarra&quot;, &quot;Valencian Community&quot;), class = &quot;factor&quot;), \r<br>    years = c(2012L, 2012L, 2012L, 2012L, 2012L, 2012L, 2012L, \r<br>    2012L, 20